Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): slow-link follow-ups: log the entry line before
 any answer, foreground plugin detail opens, document the hang cost [daveey]

Follow-up to PR #1928 (review 5887354507, non-blocking points 1-3).

1. slow-link.ts "Known costs" now also documents the second cost: a remote process that hangs while its tunnel
   stays alive looks like a slow link and is retired only after 3 probe timeouts with no answer in between (40 s
   stretched probes, requests waiting up to 60 s in between): minutes instead of ~10 s.
2. dispatchSlowLink takes the log and wires it into the tracker when the dispatch option is built, so a probe that
   times out before any remote request has answered in this process still writes the
   "[slow-link] ... is slow" entry line (noteRemoteAnswer was the only place that set it). main.ts passes
   rememberLog (one line changed, no growth).
3. A user-driven plugin GET is no longer thinned on a slow link: PluginRestOptions gains priority 'foreground'
   (pluginRest forwards it), and the Kanban task drawer tags the first task and log read of each open
   (userOpenReads; the drawer mounts once per open). Re-opening the same task within the 30 s thinning gap is
   therefore sent; the interval and socket refetches of that open stay background polls and are still thinned.
   The thinned prefixes are unchanged.

Tests (fail before, pass after): slow-link.test.ts "dispatchSlowLink logs the slow-link entry line when a probe
times out before any remote has answered" (+ main.ts wiring pin with rememberLog); plugins.test.ts priority
passthrough cases; drawer.test.tsx "tags the reads of each open foreground, so a slow link never skips a re-open;
refetches stay polls". The main-side thinner already never holds a foreground GET (existing thinnedPoll test).
